  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let the mean and the variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;observations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>194</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;respectively.&nbsp;If the mean and variance of the first <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;observation are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>",
